    {
      "id": "4a8fb9e2-9d6a-4c1e-80ed-e28af7fd94e5",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -128,
        -336
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#E1C1DE",
        "width": 320,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## \ud83d\udcdd Form: Submit Maintenance Request\n\n### Purpose\nProvides a form for residents or users to report maintenance issues and upload a photo of the damage.\n\n### How It Works\n- Collects the reporter's name.\n- Collects the apartment or room number.\n- Collects a detailed description of the issue.\n- Requires a JPG or PNG photo of the damage.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f743103f-4aa3-4e5f-ab48-e3d3f1086431",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        208,
        -368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#C6C1E1",
        "width": 352,
        "height": 512,
        "content": "## \ud83d\udd17 Create Public Photo Link\n\n### Purpose\nUploads the damage photo and generates a URL that can be used in the maintenance tracker and notification email.\n\n### How It Works\n- Receives the submitted photo from the form node.\n- Uploads the file through the UploadToURL integration.\n\n### Why It's Needed\nAllows the maintenance team to view the damage photo directly from the spreadsheet or email instead of searching for the original submission.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "38c7d783-6eb2-489f-b530-7b923f500678",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        576,
        -400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#ADCDBC",
        "width": 336,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## \ud83d\udcca Log Ticket in Database\n\n### Purpose\nStores each submitted maintenance request in Google Sheets to create a centralized maintenance ticket tracker.\n\n### Spreadsheet Columns\n- Date Reported\n- Reporter\n- Location\n- Issue Description\n- Photo Preview\n- Ticket Status\n\n### Why It's Needed\nMaintains a searchable record of maintenance requests, helping property managers organize reported issues and monitor pending work."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "58bd3c02-51b5-4ac3-b17b-6e232f78fa70",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        928,
        -240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#CDC6AD",
        "width": 320,
        "height": 384,
        "content": "## \ud83d\udce7 Email Alert to Manager\n\n### Purpose\nSends an email notification to the maintenance manager when a new repair request has been logged.\n\n### Why It's Needed\nNotifies the maintenance manager promptly so that reported issues can be reviewed and assigned for resolution."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "dfbf5356-0ee7-4199-abe3-1c3908c18f5a",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -128,
        -656
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#F0D5DF",
        "width": 768,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Automated Maintenance Ticketing System\n\n### Workflow Overview\n1. A resident submits a maintenance request through an online form.\n2. The form collects the reporter's name, apartment or room number, issue description, and damage photo.\n3. UploadToURL uploads the photo and generates a public URL.\n4. Google Sheets records the request details, photo preview, submission timestamp, and initial ticket status.\n5. Gmail sends an HTML email alert to the maintenance manager with the request details and damage photo.\n6. The manager can use the ticket tracker link to review the logged request.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
